<!--
  JURROX_MIGRATE_INTO_WARSCAR_GAUNT. The rakeshank: an ultra-gaunt stilt-legged carrion gleaner. Its picture was drawn
  as the Forge slot candidate "jurrox" (forgeslot_jurrox_v1, never a def); owner's ruling on the 2026-10-16 art sheet:
  "Wonderfully grotesque. Add it to the Warscar and make a new name and description for it based on its ultra-gaunt
  appearance." New invented name, free RM_ tier, ONE HOME: the Warscar (roster row in RM_Warscar.xml).
  Art installed through the art ledger at the texPath below (east/north/south, copied from the jurrox candidate).
  Corpse-eating is vanilla CarnivoreAnimal behaviour on a non-predator, as RM_Pallbearer does. Numbers PROVISIONAL.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Rakeshank</defName>
    <label>rakeshank</label>
    <description>A starved-looking thing on four impossibly long, thin legs, its body slung so high that the poisoned ground never touches it. The hide is pulled so tight over the frame that every rib, hip and knuckle of spine shows through, and its neck rises into a long, narrow beak it uses like tongs to pick the dead out of craters. It is not starving; it simply never fills out. Rakeshanks walk the Warscar in a slow, high-stepping trot, drifting from one old shell crater to the next in search of what the war left behind.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>4.6</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>28</Mass>
      <MarketValue>160</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.75</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-5</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>60</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <LeatherAmount>12</LeatherAmount>
      <MeatAmount>20</MeatAmount>
    </statBases>
